{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.SpectralSequenceCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.SpectralSequenceCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Ideal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.UniversalDifferentials"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.wedderburnWeight_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.wedderburnWeight_smul","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L174-L179","doc":"q-deformed Wedderburn-block weights are R-linear in `dim_q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.plancherelWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.plancherelWeight","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L167-L172","doc":"Backward-compat alias: the legacy name `plancherelWeight` is kept\nso older downstream code keeps compiling.  Prefer `wedderburnWeight`\nin new code, since the quantity is the q-deformed Wedderburn-block\nweight, **not** the (distinct) classical Plancherel measure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.wedderburnWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.wedderburnWeight","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L158-L165","doc":"**q-deformed Wedderburn-block weight on λ.**\n`tilde w_λ := dim_q²(λ) / [n]_q!`.  Bounded but `Σ_λ tilde w_λ ≠ 1`\nat q ≠ 1 in general; the classical Plancherel measure\n`w_λ := (dim V_λ)² / n!` (which does sum to 1 exactly) is the\ndistinct family — see `prop:plancherel-weight-boundedness`.\nGeneric over a commutative ring `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.centralIdempotent_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.centralIdempotent_idem","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L108-L132","doc":"**The central idempotents are idempotent.**  A re-export of the\n`SemisimpleAlgebra.e_idem` class field.\n\n**This does NOT establish the spectral-sequence collapse**, and it was\nnamed as though it did until 2026-08-26.  Read the type: the conclusion is\n`e * e = e`.  It says nothing about `E_∞`, nothing about a filtration, and\nit does not use the `[WhiteheadHH R A]` instance at all — the hypothesis\nthe collapse is supposed to turn on.  The instance is kept in the signature\nonly so the rename is behaviour-preserving for any call site that supplies\nit; it is unused, deliberately, and that is the point.\n\nHistory, because this defect was found twice: the QA drain of 2026-06-07\nreported *\"Lean only proves `e*e=e` idempotency\"*, and the 2026-06-12 drain\nclosed it as stale under a heading reading \"do NOT re-file\", on the grounds\nthat the file had since gained `SemisimpleAlgebra`, `WhiteheadHH`, a real\n`innerDerivation` and a theorem *named* `spectral_sequence_collapses_to_centre`.\nAll true; none of it changed what the theorem proves.  Corrected in\n`docs/audits/2026-06-12-qa-drain-r5r6-findings.md`; rediscovered\nindependently in `docs/audits/2026-08-25-spectral-sequence-is-a-no-go-not-a-tool.md`.\n`docs/audits/lean-triviality.json` had it flagged `\"closed\": false` throughout. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spectral-sequence-collapse","label":"prop:spectral-sequence-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH.inner_of_derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH.inner_of_derivation","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L104-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH.mk","kind":"ctor","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.WhiteheadHH","kind":"class","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**Whitehead lemma (semisimple HH¹ vanishing, axiom form).**\n\nFor a semisimple algebra `A` over a field of characteristic zero,\nevery derivation is inner.  Equivalently, `HH^1(A, A) = 0`.\n\nRecorded as conjectural-class data because Mathlib does not yet\nhave a Hochschild-cohomology framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.innerDerivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.innerDerivation","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L85-L93","doc":"Inner derivation `ad_x(a) = x·a − a·x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.existsUnique_factor_Ω1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.existsUnique_factor_Ω1","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L57-L83","doc":"**Every derivation factors uniquely through `Ω¹(A)`.**  For a\nderivation `D : A → A`, there is exactly one map `φ : Ω¹(A) → A` that is\na map of `A`-bimodules and satisfies `φ ∘ d = D`.  Here `Ω¹(A) = ker μ`\nis the universal noncommutative calculus of\n`QOU.MathlibExt.UniversalDifferentials`, the same `Ω¹` that the field\n`QuantumUniverse.differentialForms` realises in `C`.\n\nSo derivations of `A` into itself are the same thing as bimodule maps\n`Ω¹(A) → A`.  `WhiteheadHH` below is therefore a statement about maps out\nof `Ω¹(A)`.\n\n`Derivation` here is defined locally, not taken from Mathlib, because\nMathlib's `Derivation` needs a commutative algebra and the Hecke algebra\nis not commutative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.d","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.Derivation","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L50-L54","doc":"`R`-linear derivation `d : A → A` satisfying Leibniz. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_idem","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e_central","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.e","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.central_idempotents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.central_idempotents","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnMass.SemisimpleAlgebra","kind":"class","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/spectral-sequence-collapse.lean#L34-L48","doc":"**Semisimple algebra with explicit Wedderburn data.**\n\nRecords the central-idempotent decomposition `A = ⊕_i e_i · A · e_i`\nof a semisimple algebra over `R`.  This is the structural data that\nsurvives the GB-filtration spectral sequence's collapse.\n\nFor `A = H_n(R, q)` at generic `q`, the index type\n`central_idempotents` is the set of partitions `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}